{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_general_word","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_general_word","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.cycle_regime_is_below_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.cycle_regime_is_below_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":537,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L537-L547","doc":"**A cycle's own regime is below that threshold.** If the holonomy ratio is\nnear one in the sense `2^k < 2 · 3^m − 2^m` — which includes every\n`2^k ≤ 3^m`, and more generally everything up to nearly twice `3^m` — the\ncriterion is unavailable. Since a bounded cycle value forces `2^k` close to\n`3^m`, cycle candidates sit inside this regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.height_criterion_vacuous_below_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.height_criterion_vacuous_below_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L522-L535","doc":"**The height criterion is vacuous below the threshold.** If\n`2^k ≤ 2·3^m − 2^m` then no word satisfies `φ(n_w) < 2^k − 3^m`, so\n`qcollatz_no_cycle_of_height_lt` cannot fire for any word at all.\n\nComplementary to `qcollatz_no_front_loaded_cycle`, whose hypothesis at\n`D = m` is exactly `2·3^m − 2^m < 2^k`: the criterion is available above the\nthreshold and provably unavailable below it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_no_front_loaded_periodic_orbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_no_front_loaded_periodic_orbit","kind":"theorem","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L478-L491","doc":"**No front-loaded periodic orbit under the contractivity bound.** The\norbit-level form of `qcollatz_no_front_loaded_cycle`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_no_periodic_orbit_of_height_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_no_periodic_orbit_of_height_lt","kind":"theorem","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L461-L476","doc":"**No periodic orbit of any word whose exact height is below the denominator\nheight.** The orbit-level form of `qcollatz_no_cycle_of_height_lt`: the forced\ncycle equation is discharged internally, so the hypotheses are just the step\nrelation, the return `P k = P 0`, and two finite integer computations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_no_cycle_of_height_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_no_cycle_of_height_lt","kind":"theorem","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L421-L450","doc":"**General-word exclusion, by the exact height.** For *any* parity word: if the\nnumerator's height is positive and strictly below the denominator's height\n`2^k − 3^m`, the divisibility `φ(D) ∣ φ(n_w)` demanded by a cycle fails, so no\nsuch cycle exists.\n\nUnlike `qcollatz_no_front_loaded_cycle` this carries **no shape hypothesis** —\nthe criterion is evaluated directly from the word. Both hypotheses are finite\ninteger computations for a concrete `w` and `k`.\n\n**Scope (a), unchanged.** This is a criterion, not a proof that the criterion\nis always met: for a general word the height can exceed `2^k − 3^m`, and\ndeciding when it does not is the open problem. It systematises the two\nexisting families rather than superseding the question. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_closed","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L383-L419","doc":"**Exact `q = 1` height of the numerator.** Each odd step at position `i`\ncontributes `2^i`, tripled once for every odd step strictly after it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oddCount_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oddCount_mono","kind":"theorem","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L371-L381","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.front_loaded_beyond_adjacent_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.front_loaded_beyond_adjacent_tail","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L344-L354","doc":"**The hypotheses of `qcollatz_no_front_loaded_cycle` are satisfiable outside\nthe adjacent-tail family** — witnessing that the new exclusion is not vacuous\nand not a restatement of what is already proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oeoWord_oddCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oeoWord_oddCount","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L341-L342","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oeoWord_front","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oeoWord_front","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L336-L339","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oeoWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oeoWord","kind":"def","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L333-L334","doc":"The word `O E O` followed by even steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_no_front_loaded_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_no_front_loaded_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L278-L324","doc":"**No front-loaded cycle under the contractivity bound.** Suppose every odd\nstep of the word occurs before position `D`, there is at least one, and the\nperiod-`k` cycle equation is forced. Then the `q = 1` height obstruction\nfires whenever\n\n    3^m·2^D  <  2^m·2^k − 2^m·3^m + 2^m·2^D        (`m = oddCount w D`),\n\nand no such cycle exists.\n\nTaking `D = m` (all odd steps first, then evens) the hypothesis reduces to\n`2·3^m − 2^m < 2^k`, so this **subsumes** `qcollatz_no_adj_tail_cycle`, whose\nhypothesis is the very slightly stronger `2·3^m < 2^k`; every `D > m` is a\nword shape no existing lemma reaches.\n\n**Scope (a).** This excludes the front-loaded words, not all words: the\ngeneral upper bound alone forces `m ≤ 1`, and the general cycle problem is\nopen classically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_const_of_front","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_const_of_front","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L252-L276","doc":"**Past the last odd step nothing accumulates.** If every step from `D` on is\neven, the numerator and the odd-count are constant from `D` onwards. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_upper","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L218-L248","doc":"**Upper height bound `2^m·(φ(n_w) + 2^n) ≤ 3^m·2^n`**, i.e.\n`φ(n_w) ≤ 3^m·2^{n−m} − 2^n`, stated without `ℕ`-subtraction in the exponent.\nSharp: equality holds for the word whose odd steps all sit at the end. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_lower","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L196-L216","doc":"**Lower height bound `3^m ≤ φ(n_w) + 2^m`**, i.e. `φ(n_w) ≥ 3^m − 2^m`,\nstated without `ℕ`-subtraction. The bound is *attained* by the adjacent-tail\nword, whose numerator `oddTailSum` has height exactly `3^m − 2^m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L185-L194","doc":"**The numerator height is non-negative.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_succ_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_succ_even","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L176-L183","doc":"Numerator recursion at `q = 1`, even step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_succ_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum_map_succ_odd","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L165-L174","doc":"Numerator recursion at `q = 1`, odd step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordHol_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordHol_map","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L144-L163","doc":"**Holonomy height is `3^m`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_word_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.qcollatz_word_forces","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L126-L136","doc":"**General-word cycle forcing.** A period-`k` orbit of any parity word `w`\nforces `((q+1)^k − [3]_q^m)·P₀ = n_w`, the holonomy being `[3]_q^m` for `m`\nthe number of odd steps. Specialises to every named period-2/3/4 forcing\nlemma and to `qcollatz_adj_tail_forces`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.word_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.word_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L110-L124","doc":"**General-word collapse.** For any parity word `w`, an orbit satisfying the\nuniform affine step relation obeys\n`(q+1)^n · Pₙ = wordHol · P₀ + wordNum` after `n` steps. This is the\narbitrary-word generalisation of `even_chain_collapse` and\n`odd_chain_collapse`, which are its all-even and all-odd specialisations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oddCount_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oddCount_le","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L100-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oddCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.oddCount","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L95-L98","doc":"**Number of odd steps among the first `n`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordNum","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L89-L93","doc":"**Numerator after `n` steps** — the accumulated `+1`s, each carried through\nthe later odd multipliers and weighted by the `[2]_q`-power at its position. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordHol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.wordHol","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L83-L87","doc":"**Holonomy after `n` steps** — the product of the step multipliers, i.e.\n`[3]_q` raised to the number of odd steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.stepAdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.stepAdd","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L79-L81","doc":"The additive constant of step `i`: `1` on an odd step, `0` on an even step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.stepMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzGeneralWord.stepMul","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_general_word.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The multiplier of step `i`: `[3]_q` on an odd step, `1` on an even step. ","signatureChunk":0}]}